-const CONFIG={"mode":"review","type":"Comprehensive Review","block":1,"cs":"CS 1–4","title":"Civic Participation and Public Decisions Review","description":"Apply CS 1–4 through realistic scenarios, source evaluation, comparison, and cause and effect.","practice":"Ohio OST-style civic action, information literacy, and decision-making.","assignmentKey":"gov-phase2-block1-review-2026-v2"};
-const QUESTIONS=[{"id":"b1r01","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Levels","prompt":"Residents want a traffic light at a dangerous city intersection. What is the best first action?","choices":["Present the concern to city officials responsible for local streets","Petition the president to issue an executive order","Ask the U.S. Senate to ratify a treaty within the government system described","File a proposal with the Federal Reserve"],"answer":0,"hint":"Match the problem to the level that manages city streets.","explanation":"A city traffic issue belongs first with local government."},{"id":"b1r02","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Levels","prompt":"A proposed Ohio law would change school funding. Which action best matches the issue?","choices":["Address only the local parks department","Contact members of the Ohio General Assembly","Ask the Supreme Court to write a new law","Contact foreign diplomats about a treaty"],"answer":1,"hint":"A state bill is decided by state legislators.","explanation":"The Ohio General Assembly makes state law."},{"id":"b1r03","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Levels","prompt":"Citizens object to a presidential executive order. Whom should they petition?","choices":["A township trustee handling local roads","The mayor of one Ohio city","The president and federal executive branch","A county park advisory board"],"answer":2,"hint":"Identify the official who issued the order.","explanation":"Executive orders come from the president."},{"id":"b1r04","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Participation","prompt":"A city council is considering a recycling ordinance. Which response is most direct?","choices":["Campaign against a U.S. senator in another election","Ask the governor to negotiate a treaty","Send the issue to the Federal Reserve","Speak during public comment at the city council meeting"],"answer":3,"hint":"The council will decide the ordinance.","explanation":"Public comment reaches the responsible local lawmakers before the decision."},{"id":"b1r05","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Participation","prompt":"A neighborhood park is covered with litter. Which action best demonstrates direct civic participation?","choices":["Organize residents for a volunteer cleanup and contact the parks department","Wait for a presidential campaign to address it within the government system described","Ask Congress to amend the Constitution","Request an international court ruling"],"answer":0,"hint":"Citizens can act locally while coordinating with local government.","explanation":"Volunteering and contacting the local department directly address the community problem."},{"id":"b1r06","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Statewide Action","prompt":"Ohio citizens want to propose a statewide statute directly to voters. What must they begin doing?","choices":["Ask one mayor to enact the law statewide","Organize an initiative petition and collect valid signatures","Request a federal judge to place it on the ballot","Hold a private party meeting with no petition"],"answer":1,"hint":"Ohio allows citizen-initiated statutes through petitions.","explanation":"Qualifying petition signatures begin the statewide initiative process."},{"id":"b1r07","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Elections","prompt":"A voter believes a U.S. senator should be replaced. Which action is most appropriate?","choices":["Ask a city council to remove the senator","Demand that a state court write a replacement law","Campaign and vote for an opposing Senate candidate","Petition a county agency to negotiate a treaty"],"answer":2,"hint":"Senators are chosen in elections.","explanation":"Campaigning and voting are direct electoral responses."},{"id":"b1r08","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Levels","prompt":"Which pairing correctly matches an action with its main government level?","choices":["Join the National Guard—local; contact a mayor—federal","Petition the president—state; attend city council—federal","Contact a U.S. senator—local; contact a mayor—state","Attend a township meeting—local; contact the governor—state"],"answer":3,"hint":"Identify the jurisdiction of each official or body.","explanation":"Townships are local governments; governors lead state executive branches."},{"id":"b1r09","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Choosing Action","prompt":"Why is matching civic action to government level important?","choices":["It directs citizen effort toward officials with authority over the issue","It guarantees every request will become law within the government system described","It eliminates the need to evaluate information","It prevents citizens from joining organizations"],"answer":0,"hint":"Authority differs by jurisdiction.","explanation":"An action is more effective when aimed at the body with legal power to respond."},{"id":"b1r10","cs":"CS 1","topic":"Cause and Effect","prompt":"What is a likely effect when citizens consistently attend local meetings and comment on proposals?","choices":["Federal courts automatically overturn local ordinances under the constitutional process in the question","Officials receive community input before making local decisions","Political parties stop nominating candidates","All disagreements disappear from the community"],"answer":1,"hint":"Public participation supplies information and viewpoints.","explanation":"Meeting participation can shape officials' understanding and choices."},{"id":"b1r11","cs":"CS 2","topic":"Political Parties","prompt":"A citizen wants to help elect candidates who share a broad platform. Which organization best fits?","choices":["A trial jury","A city building department","A political party","A scholarly journal"],"answer":2,"hint":"This group nominates and supports candidates.","explanation":"Political parties organize electoral efforts around candidates and platforms."},{"id":"b1r12","cs":"CS 2","topic":"Interest Groups","prompt":"A resident mainly wants to influence clean-water regulations. Which choice is most focused?","choices":["Join a court and issue a ruling when applied through ordinary legal procedures","Ask a newspaper to enact the regulation","Become a member of every political party","Join an environmental interest group that advocates on water policy"],"answer":3,"hint":"Choose a group centered on one policy concern.","explanation":"Interest groups organize around shared issues and try to influence policy."},{"id":"b1r13","cs":"CS 2","topic":"News Media","prompt":"Which action best shows the news media acting as a government watchdog?","choices":["Investigating records and reporting evidence of misuse of public funds","Appointing a cabinet secretary within the government system described within the government system described","Enforcing a court sentence","Ratifying a treaty"],"answer":0,"hint":"Watchdogs monitor powerful institutions.","explanation":"Investigative reporting can expose misconduct and support accountability."},{"id":"b1r14","cs":"CS 2","topic":"Comparison","prompt":"How do parties and interest groups differ?","choices":["Parties interpret laws; interest groups enforce them","Parties seek to elect candidates and govern broadly; interest groups focus on influencing particular issues","Parties operate only locally; interest groups operate only nationally under the constitutional process in the question","Parties publish only facts; interest groups publish only laws"],"answer":1,"hint":"Compare their main goals.","explanation":"Parties compete for governing power, while interest groups emphasize policy influence."},{"id":"b1r15","cs":"CS 2","topic":"Cause and Effect","prompt":"What is a likely result when civic groups organize many citizens around an issue?","choices":["The Constitution is automatically amended","Courts lose all authority over laws","Officials may receive more attention, information, and pressure about the policy","The issue no longer requires public decisions as an action taken by public officials"],"answer":2,"hint":"Groups combine voices and resources.","explanation":"Organized participation can make citizen concerns more visible and influential."},{"id":"b1r16","cs":"CS 2","topic":"Media Literacy","prompt":"Which use of news media is most responsible before an election?","choices":["Share the first dramatic claim without checking when applied through ordinary legal procedures","Treat every editorial as an official law","Ignore corrections published by reliable outlets","Compare reporting and evidence from several credible sources"],"answer":3,"hint":"Citizens should verify rather than rely on one claim.","explanation":"Comparing credible sources helps voters make informed choices."},{"id":"b1r17","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Verification","prompt":"A viral post claims the state canceled an election. What should a citizen do first?","choices":["Check the state election office and corroborate the claim with credible reporting","Share it quickly so others can react within the government system described","Assume repetition makes it accurate","Use an anonymous comment as final proof"],"answer":0,"hint":"Look for an official source and independent confirmation.","explanation":"High-impact claims should be verified using reliable, independent evidence."},{"id":"b1r18","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Source Types","prompt":"Which source is best for expert research about the economic effect of a tax proposal?","choices":["An unsigned meme with no cited evidence","A peer-reviewed study by qualified economists using transparent data","A campaign slogan repeated in an advertisement","A rumor from an unrelated social-media account under the constitutional process in the question"],"answer":1,"hint":"Expertise and checkable methods matter.","explanation":"Peer-reviewed research with transparent evidence is the strongest option listed."},{"id":"b1r19","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Source Types","prompt":"What does a transcript of sworn court testimony provide?","choices":["A guarantee that every statement is correct as an action taken by public officials","A neutral summary of all later scholarship","A record of what a witness said under oath in the case","A law automatically enacted by the court"],"answer":2,"hint":"Testimony is evidence, but it still must be evaluated.","explanation":"The transcript preserves the witness's statement; it does not guarantee truth."},{"id":"b1r20","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Fact and Opinion","prompt":"Which statement is most clearly an opinion?","choices":["The council voted 5–2 on Tuesday","The proposal costs $2 million in the adopted budget when applied through ordinary legal procedures","The meeting lasted ninety minutes","The council made the worst possible choice for the city"],"answer":3,"hint":"Look for a value judgment.","explanation":"Calling a choice the worst is a judgment rather than a directly verifiable fact."},{"id":"b1r21","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Evidence","prompt":"A group claims a new arena will produce more revenue than it costs. Which evidence is most useful?","choices":["Independent projections of construction costs, operating costs, and expected revenue","The size of the crowd at one rally within the government system described","A slogan printed by the development campaign","The personal preference of one athlete"],"answer":0,"hint":"Compare measurable costs and benefits.","explanation":"Independent financial projections directly test the economic claim."},{"id":"b1r22","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Bias","prompt":"A source has a clear viewpoint. What should a careful reader do?","choices":["Reject every statement without checking","Examine its evidence and compare it with independent credible sources","Accept every claim because the viewpoint is clear under the constitutional process in the question","Replace evidence with a preferred opinion"],"answer":1,"hint":"Bias calls for evaluation, not automatic acceptance or rejection.","explanation":"Readers should inspect support, purpose, and corroboration."},{"id":"b1r23","cs":"CS 3","topic":"Currency","prompt":"Why does the publication date matter when evaluating election information?","choices":["Older sources can never contain useful facts as an action ta