c interest can shape how branches prioritize issues.</p></section><section class="question-panel" id="q28"><h2>Informal relations · 28</h2><p>Informal working relationships can support policy cooperation.</p></section><section class="question-panel" id="q29"><h2>Synthesis · 29</h2><p>Government policy emerges from branch responsibilities, checks, cooperation, and political context.</p></section><section class="question-panel" id="q30"><h2>Application · 30</h2><p>Identifying actors and effects reveals the relevant power or check.</p></section></main></html>
