-const QUESTIONS=[{"id":"q01","cs":"CS 14 • Rights","topic":"CS 14 • Rights","prompt":"Which statement best defines a constitutional right?","choices":["a protected claim against undue government interference","a reward granted by a business within the government system described","an optional school policy","a tax collected by a city"],"answer":0,"hint":"Think protection from government intrusion.","explanation":"Rights protect areas of liberty and participation."},{"id":"q02","cs":"CS 14 • Participation","topic":"CS 14 • Participation","prompt":"A citizen speaks at a council meeting. Which right supports this action?","choices":["double jeopardy under the constitutional process in the question","freedom of speech","presidential succession","appellate jurisdiction"],"answer":1,"hint":"The citizen is expressing an opinion.","explanation":"Speech protects political participation."},{"id":"q03","cs":"CS 14 • Participation","topic":"CS 14 • Participation","prompt":"A newspaper investigates public corruption. Which right is central?","choices":["right to bear arms","right to counsel","freedom of the press","reserved powers"],"answer":2,"hint":"Think journalism.","explanation":"Press freedom supports public accountability."},{"id":"q04","cs":"CS 14 • Participation","topic":"CS 14 • Participation","prompt":"Citizens gather peacefully to support a cause. Which right applies?","choices":["due process only","term limits","judicial review","freedom of assembly"],"answer":3,"hint":"They are gathering.","explanation":"Assembly protects peaceful group participation."},{"id":"q05","cs":"CS 14 • Participation","topic":"CS 14 • Participation","prompt":"Citizens ask legislators to change a policy. Which right applies?","choices":["right to petition","right to jury trial","protection from search","right to pardon"],"answer":0,"hint":"They are making a request to government.","explanation":"Petition supports direct public input."},{"id":"q06","cs":"CS 14 • Incorporation","topic":"CS 14 • Incorporation","prompt":"A state government violates a protected freedom in the Bill of Rights. Which doctrine may make that protection applicable?","choices":["federalism only","incorporation","executive privilege","senatorial courtesy"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think Fourteenth Amendment due process.","explanation":"Incorporation applies most Bill of Rights guarantees to states."},{"id":"q07","cs":"CS 14 • Incorporation","topic":"CS 14 • Incorporation","prompt":"Which amendment provides the due process foundation for incorporation?","choices":["Tenth Amendment","Twelfth Amendment","Fourteenth Amendment","Twenty-second Amendment"],"answer":2,"hint":"This amendment also contains equal protection.","explanation":"The Supreme Court uses Fourteenth Amendment due process."},{"id":"q08","cs":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","topic":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","prompt":"A citizen exercises free speech while listening respectfully to disagreement. What responsibility is shown?","choices":["military command","jury nullification","executive enforcement","civil discourse"],"answer":3,"hint":"Rights should respect others.","explanation":"Civil discourse is a responsibility connected to speech."},{"id":"q09","cs":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","topic":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","prompt":"Which responsibility is most directly connected to the right to bear arms?","choices":["receiving firearms training","registering to vote","serving on a jury","paying a poll tax"],"answer":0,"hint":"Think safe exercise of the right.","explanation":"Training promotes responsible firearm use."},{"id":"q10","cs":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","topic":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","prompt":"Which responsibility supports the right to a jury trial?","choices":["filing court appeals under the constitutional process in the question","serving on juries when called","issuing pardons","signing treaties"],"answer":1,"hint":"The system needs citizens as jurors.","explanation":"Jury service helps provide jury trials."},{"id":"q11","cs":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","topic":"CS 14 • Responsibilities","prompt":"Which actions responsibly support voting?","choices":["avoiding all public issues","paying a poll tax","registering and becoming informed","refusing election information"],"answer":2,"hint":"Participation requires preparation.","explanation":"Registration and informed choice support meaningful suffrage."},{"id":"q12","cs":"CS 14 • General duties","topic":"CS 14 • General duties","prompt":"Which is a general responsibility of citizenship?","choices":["ignoring taxes","denying others’ rights when applied through ordinary legal procedures","avoiding responsibility","respecting the rule of law"],"answer":3,"hint":"Everyone must follow valid law.","explanation":"Rule-of-law respect is a general responsibility."},{"id":"q13","cs":"CS 14 • General duties","topic":"CS 14 • General duties","prompt":"Why are paying taxes and fees civic responsibilities?","choices":["they help fund government services and functions","they eliminate constitutional rights within the government system described","they select federal judges","they replace elections"],"answer":0,"hint":"Government services require revenue.","explanation":"Taxes support public functions."},{"id":"q14","cs":"CS 14 • Service","topic":"CS 14 • Service","prompt":"Which is service to the nation or state?","choices":["private entertainment","military service community service or public office","avoiding elections","refusing every jury summons under the constitutional process in the question"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think contributions beyond personal benefit.","explanation":"Citizens may serve through military, community, or office."},{"id":"q15","cs":"CS 14 • Relative rights","topic":"CS 14 • Relative rights","prompt":"Why are individual rights described as relative rather than absolute?","choices":["government may eliminate any right as an action taken by public officials","rights apply only during elections","their exercise must be balanced with others’ rights and the common good","only majorities possess rights"],"answer":2,"hint":"One person’s exercise can affect others.","explanation":"Rights have lawful limits protecting others and society."},{"id":"q16","cs":"CS 15 • Majority rule","topic":"CS 15 • Majority rule","prompt":"What problem can arise from majority rule without minority protections?","choices":["courts lose all jurisdiction when applied through ordinary legal procedures","taxes automatically disappear","presidents gain unlimited terms","the majority may deny rights to a smaller group"],"answer":3,"hint":"Numbers do not erase rights.","explanation":"Constitutional government balances majority decisions with minority rights."},{"id":"q17","cs":"CS 15 • Suffrage","topic":"CS 15 • Suffrage","prompt":"Which amendment extended suffrage regardless of sex?","choices":["Nineteenth Amendment","Thirteenth Amendment","Twenty-second Amendment","Twenty-fifth Amendment"],"answer":0,"hint":"Think women’s suffrage.","explanation":"The Nineteenth Amendment prohibited sex-based voting denial."},{"id":"q18","cs":"CS 15 • Poll tax","topic":"CS 15 • Poll tax","prompt":"Which amendment eliminated poll taxes in federal elections?","choices":["Fifteenth Amendment","Twenty-fourth Amendment","Nineteenth Amendment","Twenty-sixth Amendment"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think voting fees.","explanation":"The Twenty-fourth Amendment removed a financial voting barrier."},{"id":"q19","cs":"CS 15 • Executive","topic":"CS 15 • Executive","prompt":"Federal troops protect students integrating a public school. Which branch is acting?","choices":["legislative branch","judicial branch only","executive branch","local legislative branch"],"answer":2,"hint":"The president commands federal enforcement.","explanation":"Executive action helped enforce integration at Little Rock."},{"id":"q20","cs":"CS 15 • Executive","topic":"CS 15 • Executive","prompt":"Federal officials prosecute violations of open-housing law. Which branch role is illustrated?","choices":["judicial lawmaking","legislative appeal","state ratification","executive enforcement"],"answer":3,"hint":"Prosecution carries out law.","explanation":"The executive enforces civil-rights legislation."},{"id":"q21","cs":"CS 15 • Legislative","topic":"CS 15 • Legislative","prompt":"Congress passes a law banning discrimination in public accommodations. Which branch extended rights?","choices":["legislative branch","executive branch","judicial branch","Electoral College"],"answer":0,"hint":"Congress enacts statutes.","explanation":"Civil rights acts are legislative action."},{"id":"q22","cs":"CS 15 • Legislative","topic":"CS 15 • Legislative","prompt":"Congress protects access to the ballot through a federal statute. Which action is this?","choices":["executive pardon under the constitutional process in the question","Voting Rights Act legislation","judicial nomination","constitutional veto"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think congressional voting protection.","explanation":"The Voting Rights Act used legislative power."},{"id":"q23","cs":"CS 15 • Judicial","topic":"CS 15 • Judicial","prompt":"The Supreme Court applies a Bill of Rights protection to a state. Which process is used?","choices":["impeachment","referendum","incorporation","taxation"],"answer":2,"hint":"Think Fourteenth Amendment.","explanation":"Incorporation extends most federal guarantees to states."},{"id":"q24","cs":"CS 15 • Judicial","topic":"CS 15 • Judicial","prompt":"A court strikes down a discriminatory state law under equal protection. Which branch acts?","choices":["executive branch","legislative branch","county commission","judicial branch"],"answer":3,"hint":"A court is interpreting the Constitution.","explanation":"Judicial review and equal protection can extend civil rights."},{"id":"q25","cs":"CS 15 • Public pressure","topic":"CS 15 • Public pressure","prompt":"Why does public pressure matter in civil-rights history?","choices":["it can push government branches to protect denied rights","it automatically amends the Constitution within the government system described","it replaces every election","it removes judicial independence"],"answer":0,"hint":"People can demand action.","explanation":"Organizing and advocacy can prompt government response."},{"id":"q26","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows executive action expanding participation?","choices":["Congress passing a statute","troops enforcing school integration","a court interpreting equal protection","a state collecting taxes"],"answer":1,"hint":"Identify the president’s branch.","explanation":"Federal troops were an executive enforcement action."},{"id":"q27","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows legislative action expanding civil rights?","choices":["granting a pardon","deciding a court appeal as an action taken by public officials","enacting civil rights and voting rights laws","commanding federal troops"],"answer":2,"hint":"Congress makes laws.","explanation":"Congress enacted statutory protections."},{"id":"q28","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows judicial action expanding civil rights?","choices":["collecting taxes","negotiating a treaty when applied through ordinary legal procedures","organizing a campaign","applying federal rights to states through incorporation"],"answer":3,"hint":"Courts interpret the Fourteenth Amendment.","explanation":"Incorporation is judicial constitutional interpretation."},{"id":"q29","cs":"CS 14–15 • Cause and effect","topic":"CS 14–15 • Cause and effect","prompt":"Which relationship is correct?","choices":["Denial of minority rights created pressure for federal action to expand protection.","Civil rights laws caused Jim Crow to begin. within the government system described","Incorporation removed the Bill of Rights.","Jury service ended voting rights."],"answer":0,"hint":"Connect injustice to reform.","explanation":"Federal branches responded over time to exclusion and public pressure."},{"id":"q30","cs":"CS 14–15 • Synthesis","topic":"CS 14–15 • Synthesis","prompt":"Which statement best summarizes the block?","choices":["Rights require no responsibilities or limits. under the constitutional process in the question","Rights depend on responsible exercise and government protection against majority abuse.","Only states protect civil rights.","Majorities may always cancel minority rights."],"answer":1,"hint":"Combine responsibility and protection.","explanation":"Citizens and institutions both help sustain rights."},{"id":"q31","cs":"CS 14–15 • Application","topic":"CS 14–15 • Application","prompt":"A scenario asks how a right and responsibility connect. What should you identify?","choices":["only the amendment number as an action taken by public officials as an action taken by public officials","the longest answer choice","the protected liberty and the conduct needed to respect others or the common good","the political party involved"],"answer":2,"hint":"Match freedom with responsible use.","explanation":"The standard requires explaining the relationship."},{"id":"q32","cs":"CS 14–15 • Application","topic":"CS 14–15 • Application","prompt":"A minority group is denied participation. What evidence best answers how government responded?","choices":["a private purchase","an unrelated tax change when applied through ordinary legal procedures when applied through ordinary legal procedures","a weather report","a specific amendment law executive action or court ruling that expanded access"],"answer":3,"hint":"Use a branch or constitutional action.","explanation":"A strong response identifies denial and the government remedy."}];
