lation?","choices":["general rise in prices over time","government spending exceeding revenue","expense a business incurs to follow regulations","share of deposits banks must hold rather than lend"],"answer":0,"hint":"Think about how inflation is used in this unit.","explanation":"inflation means general rise in prices over time."},{"id":"test-language-1","cs":"State Test Language","topic":"State Test Language","prompt":"What is a tax deduction?","choices":["a direct payment added to every worker’s wages","an allowed amount subtracted before taxable income is calculated","an interest-rate increase ordered by Congress","a fee charged whenever a person votes"],"answer":1,"hint":"A deduction reduces the income on which tax is calculated.","explanation":"A tax deduction lowers taxable income; it is not the same as a direct payment."},{"id":"test-language-2","cs":"State Test Language","topic":"State Test Language","prompt":"What are unemployment benefits?","choices":["permanent salaries paid to every adult citizen as an action taken by public officials","loans issued only to private corporations","temporary payments to eligible workers who lose jobs through no fault of their own","tax penalties imposed on unemployed workers"],"answer":2,"hint":"These payments help eligible workers while they look for work.","explanation":"Unemployment benefits temporarily replace part of lost wages for eligible workers."},{"id":"test-language-3","cs":"State Test Language","topic":"State Test Language","prompt":"What is disposable income?","choices":["all revenue collected by the federal government","money banks must keep as required reserves","the total value of goods produced nationally","income remaining after required taxes are paid"],"answer":3,"hint":"This is money available to spend or save.","explanation":"Disposable income is what remains after required taxes."}];
