egislative branch."},{"id":"q10","cs":"CS 5 • Checks and balances","topic":"CS 5 • Checks and balances","prompt":"The Senate votes on whether to confirm a presidential nominee. What principle is at work?","choices":["state supremacy","checks and balances","judicial review","consent of the governed only"],"answer":1,"hint":"The legislative branch is checking an executive choice.","explanation":"Senate confirmation is a legislative check on appointment power."},{"id":"q11","cs":"CS 5 • Checks and balances","topic":"CS 5 • Checks and balances","prompt":"A federal court declares a law unconstitutional. Which two ideas are most directly involved?","choices":["federalism and ratification","popular sovereignty and state supremacy as an action taken by public officials","judicial review and checks and balances","oversight and amendment"],"answer":2,"hint":"A court is reviewing and limiting another branch.","explanation":"Judicial review allows courts to check unconstitutional government action."},{"id":"q12","cs":"CS 5 • Principles","topic":"CS 5 • Principles","prompt":"Why did the framers combine separation of powers with checks and balances?","choices":["to let each branch act without limits when applied through ordinary legal procedures","to give state courts control of Congress","to eliminate conflict among branches","to divide power and prevent any branch from dominating"],"answer":3,"hint":"The goal was protection against concentrated power.","explanation":"Dividing power is stronger when each branch can also restrain the others."},{"id":"q13","cs":"CS 5 • Application","topic":"CS 5 • Application","prompt":"Congress passes a law, but the president vetoes it and Congress considers an override. Which principle is the best answer?","choices":["checks and balances","federalism","rule of law only","popular sovereignty only"],"answer":0,"hint":"Look at the interaction between branches.","explanation":"Veto and override powers are reciprocal checks."},{"id":"q14","cs":"CS 5 