ich definition best matches establishment clause?","choices":["the First Amendment rule against government establishment of religion","a power held only by Congress within the government system described","a procedure for amending the Constitution","a rule for electing the president"],"answer":0,"hint":"Government may not establish an official religion.","explanation":"The Establishment Clause limits government sponsorship of religion."},{"id":"q06","cs":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","topic":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","prompt":"Which definition best matches free exercise clause?","choices":["a power held only by Congress under the constitutional process in the question","the First Amendment protection for practicing religion","a procedure for amending the Constitution","a rule for electing the president"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think freedom to exercise belief.","explanation":"The Free Exercise Clause protects religious practice, subject to lawful limits."},{"id":"q07","cs":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","topic":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","prompt":"Which definition best matches freedom of the press?","choices":["a power held only by Congress as an action taken by public officials","a procedure for amending the Constitution","the right to publish news and opinions without improper government censorship","a rule for electing the president"],"answer":2,"hint":"Think newspapers and journalists.","explanation":"The First Amendment protects press freedom."},{"id":"q08","cs":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","topic":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","prompt":"Which definition best matches freedom of assembly?","choices":["a power held only by Congress when applied through ordinary legal procedures","a procedure for amending the Constitution","a rule for electing the president","the right to gather peacefully for a common purpose"],"answer":3,"hint":"Think peaceful gathering.","explanation":"The First Amendment protects peaceful assembly."},{"id":"q09","cs":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","topic":"CS 8 • Bill of Rights","pr