oices":["a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution when applied through ordinary legal procedures","the requirement that states provide equal protection of the laws to all persons"],"answer":3,"hint":"Think equal treatment under law.","explanation":"The Equal Protection Clause is part of the Fourteenth Amendment."},{"id":"q09","cs":"CS 9 • Reconstruction","topic":"CS 9 • Reconstruction","prompt":"Which definition best matches previous condition of servitude?","choices":["a person’s former status as an enslaved person","a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution within the government system described"],"answer":0,"hint":"Servitude refers to enslavement.","explanation":"The Fifteenth Amendment forbids voting discrimination based on former enslavement."},{"id":"q10","cs":"CS 9 • Continued struggle","topic":"CS 9 • Continued struggle","prompt":"Which definition best matches Jim Crow laws?","choices":["a power exercised only by state courts","state and local laws that enforced racial segregation and inequality","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution under the constitutional process in the question"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think segregation after Reconstruction.","explanation":"Jim Crow laws limited African American equality despite the Reconstruction Amendments."},{"id":"q11","cs":"CS 9 • Continued struggle","topic":"CS 9 • Continued struggle","prompt":"Which definition best matches racial segregation?","choices":["a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","the enforced separation of people by race","a protection found only in the original Constitution"],"answer":2,"hint":"Think separate facilities and institutions.","explanation":"Jim Crow used segregation to maintain racial inequality."