hich definition best matches Twenty-sixth Amendment?","choices":["a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution when applied through ordinary legal procedures","the amendment protecting voting rights for citizens age eighteen and older"],"answer":3,"hint":"Think the voting age.","explanation":"The Twenty-sixth Amendment lowered the voting age to 18."},{"id":"q17","cs":"CS 10 • Suffrage","topic":"CS 10 • Suffrage","prompt":"Which definition best matches poll tax?","choices":["a fee required as a condition for voting","a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution"],"answer":0,"hint":"A tax became a voting barrier.","explanation":"Poll taxes especially burdened poor voters and were used to suppress African American voting."},{"id":"q18","cs":"CS 11 • Electoral College","topic":"CS 11 • Electoral College","prompt":"Which definition best matches Electoral College?","choices":["a power exercised only by state courts","the state-based system used to formally select the president and vice president","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a protection found only in the original Constitution under the constitutional process in the question"],"answer":1,"hint":"Think electoral votes rather than one direct national count.","explanation":"Presidents are formally selected through electoral votes from the states."},{"id":"q19","cs":"CS 11 • Electoral College","topic":"CS 11 • Electoral College","prompt":"Which definition best matches electoral vote?","choices":["a power exercised only by state courts","a method for passing ordinary legislation","a formal vote cast for president and vice president through the Electoral College","a protection found only in the original Constitution as an action taken by public officials"],"answer":2,"hint":"States receive a number of these votes.","explanation":