ts","it automatically amends the Constitution within the government system described","it replaces every election","it removes judicial independence"],"answer":0,"hint":"People can demand action.","explanation":"Organizing and advocacy can prompt government response."},{"id":"q26","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows executive action expanding participation?","choices":["Congress passing a statute","troops enforcing school integration","a court interpreting equal protection","a state collecting taxes"],"answer":1,"hint":"Identify the president’s branch.","explanation":"Federal troops were an executive enforcement action."},{"id":"q27","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows legislative action expanding civil rights?","choices":["granting a pardon","deciding a court appeal as an action taken by public officials","enacting civil rights and voting rights laws","commanding federal troops"],"answer":2,"hint":"Congress makes laws.","explanation":"Congress enacted statutory protections."},{"id":"q28","cs":"CS 15 • Analysis","topic":"CS 15 • Analysis","prompt":"Which example best shows judicial action expanding civil rights?","choices":["collecting taxes","negotiating a treaty when applied through ordinary legal procedures","organizing a campaign","applying federal rights to states through incorporation"],"answer":3,"hint":"Courts interpret the Fourteenth Amendment.","explanation":"Incorporation is judicial constitutional interpretation."},{"id":"q29","cs":"CS 14–15 • Cause and effect","topic":"CS 14–15 • Cause and effect","prompt":"Which relationship is correct?","choices":["Denial of minority rights created pressure for federal action to expand protection.","Civil rights laws caused Jim Crow to begin. within the government system described","Incorporation removed the Bill of Rights.","Jury service ended voting rights."],"answer":0,"hint":"Connect injustice to reform.","explanation":"Federal branches responded over time to exclusion and public pressure."},{"id":"q30","cs":"CS 14–15 • Synthesis","topic":"CS 14–15 • Synthesis","prompt":"Which statement best summarizes the block?","choices":["Rights require no responsibilities or limits. under the constitutional process in the question","Rights depend on responsible exercise and government protection against majority abuse.","Only states protect civil rights.","Majorities may always cancel minority rights."],"answer":1,"hint":"Combine responsibility and protection.","explanation":"Citizens and institutions both help sustain rights."},{"id":"q31","cs":"CS 14–15 • Application","topic":"CS 14–15 • Application","prompt":"A scenario asks how a right and responsibility connect. What should you identify?","choices":["only the amendment number as an action taken by public officials as an action taken by public officials","the longest answer choice","the protected liberty and the conduct needed to respect others or the common good","the political party involved"],"answer":2,"hint":"Match freedom with responsible use.","explanation":"The standard requires explaining the relationship."},{"id":"q32","cs":"CS 14–15 • Application","topic":"CS 14–15 • Application","prompt":"A minority group is denied participation. What evidence best answers how government responded?","choices":["a private purchase","an unrelated tax change when applied through ordinary legal procedures when applied through ordinary legal procedures","a weather report","a specific amendment law executive action or court ruling that expanded access"],"answer":3,"hint":"Use a branch or constitutional action.","explanation":"A strong response identifies denial and the government remedy."}];
