 federal courts."],"answer":1,"hint":"Think division of power.","explanation":"The Tenth Amendment confirms that the federal government has limited delegated powers."},{"id":"q31","cs":"Tenth Amendment • Vocabulary","topic":"Tenth Amendment • Vocabulary","prompt":"What does delegated mean in the Tenth Amendment context?","choices":["prohibited to all governments as an action taken by public officials","reserved only to cities","granted to the federal government by the Constitution","created by a newspaper"],"answer":2,"hint":"Delegated means given.","explanation":"Delegated powers are constitutionally granted to the United States."},{"id":"q32","cs":"Mixed • Amendment choice","topic":"Mixed • Amendment choice","prompt":"Police conduct an unjustified search, then prosecutors force the suspect to testify against himself. Which amendments are involved in order?","choices":["First Amendment, then Second Amendment","Sixth Amendment, then Tenth Amendment","Eighth Amendment, then First Amendment","Fourth Amendment, then Fifth Amendment"],"answer":3,"hint":"Search first; forced self-incrimination second.","explanation":"The Fourth protects against unreasonable search; the Fifth protects against compelled self-incrimination."},{"id":"q33","cs":"Mixed • Amendment choice","topic":"Mixed • Amendment choice","prompt":"A protester is arrested for a peaceful speech and later denied a lawyer at the criminal trial. Which amendments are involved?","choices":["First Amendment and Sixth Amendment","Second Amendment and Fourth Amendment","Fifth Amendment and Tenth Amendment","Eighth Amendment and Tenth Amendment"],"answer":0,"hint":"Speech first; criminal defense second.","explanation":"The First protects speech and the Sixth protects counsel."},{"id":"q34","cs":"Mixed • Government limits","topic":"Mixed • Government limits","prompt":"Which scenario best demonstrates the Bill of Rights limiting federal government?","choices":["A private store changes its hours. under the constitutional 