onal text did not erase resistance and discriminatory enforcement.","explanation":"Jim Crow and other practices undermined constitutional protections for generations."},{"id":"q09","cs":"CS 9 • Jim Crow","topic":"CS 9 • Jim Crow","prompt":"A state requires racially separate public facilities. Which historical system does this represent?","choices":["Jim Crow segregation","the Electoral College","presidential succession","birthright citizenship"],"answer":0,"hint":"Think enforced racial separation after Reconstruction.","explanation":"Jim Crow laws enforced segregation despite the Fourteenth Amendment."},{"id":"q10","cs":"CS 9 • Analysis","topic":"CS 9 • Analysis","prompt":"Which conclusion is best supported by the history of Reconstruction and Jim Crow?","choices":["An amendment always produces instant equality.","Constitutional protections may require enforcement and continued struggle to become reality.","States automatically follow every amendment without conflict. under the constitutional process in the question","Voting rights alone ended segregation."],"answer":1,"hint":"Compare the legal changes with what happened afterward.","explanation":"The gap between constitutional promise and lived equality persisted."},{"id":"q11","cs":"CS 10 • Fifteenth Amendment","topic":"CS 10 • Fifteenth Amendment","prompt":"Which voting-rights amendment prohibits racial discrimination in voting?","choices":["Nineteenth Amendment","Twenty-fourth Amendment","Fifteenth Amendment","Twenty-sixth Amendment"],"answer":2,"hint":"This amendment was part of Reconstruction.","explanation":"The Fifteenth Amendment protects voting regardless of race, color, or previous servitude."},{"id":"q12","cs":"CS 10 • Nineteenth Amendment","topic":"CS 10 • Nineteenth Amendment","prompt":"A state refuses to let women vote solely because they are women. Which amendment applies?","choices":["Fifteenth Amendment","Twenty-fourth Amendment","Twenty-sixth Amendment","Nineteenth Amendment"],"answer":3,"hint":"T